...context... many young people were sent into the arena. The film is based on the novel by Suzanne Collins, published in 2025. Joseph Zada plays the young Haymitch. McKenna Grace plays Maysilee Donner, his fellow tribute from District 12. Ralph Fiennes plays the young President Snow. Francis Lawrence, who directed the earlier Hunger Games films, directs this one too. Fans of the first films will know what happens next: Haymitch wins the 50th Games — and becomes the tired, funny, clever mentor of the later stories, played in the first films by Woody Harrelson. This film shows how he got there: a boy from District 12, in the cruellest Games of all. And on the small screen? On Monday, November 16, at 9 p.m., “I'm a Celebrity... Get Me Out of Here!” returns to ITV1 and ITVX. Ant and Dec are back in the Aus
